<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19548" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gestor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id.. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A tale-bearer</i>, <i>tattler</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homines qui gestant quique auscultant crimina,
					Si meo arbitratu liceat, omnes pendeant, Gestores linguis,
					auditores auribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 5, 12</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A manager</i>, <i>performer</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">negotiorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					49, 1, 24</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
